# Copy this file to .env and fill in your values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is git-ignored. The agent loads it itself at startup (python-dotenv),
# so it works the same from VS Code or a terminal. Variables already set in
# the environment take precedence over this file. Use plain KEY=value lines:
# no "export", no spaces around "=".

# Required. Get a key from https://console.anthropic.com
# The agent always calls https://api.anthropic.com with this key. Gateway
# settings such as ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN and ANTHROPIC_MODEL
# are ignored; choose the model with --model.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: Azure credentials for the Azure Advisor MCP server. Without these
# the server uses the "az login" session in your home directory
# (AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS defaults to AzureCliCredential). Every set AZURE_*
# variable is passed on to the server (it starts with a minimal environment
# otherwise). Do not set AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS to "dev" or leave it empty
# unless you accept that the server may hang on Linux while it looks for an X
# display (see the "Credentials" section in src/advisor_agent/azure_mcp.py).
# Service principal setup (the credential has to be named, or "az login" is
# used instead):
# AZURE_TOKEN_CREDENTIALS=EnvironmentCredential
# AZURE_TENANT_ID=
# AZURE_CLIENT_ID=
# AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Optional: Jira MCP server. Without these the agent prints a warning and runs
# with only the Azure Advisor MCP server. Set JIRA_URL plus either
# JIRA_USERNAME + JIRA_API_TOKEN (Jira Cloud) or JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN
# (Jira Server/Data Center).
# JIRA_URL=https://your-site.atlassian.net
# JIRA_USERNAME=you@example.com
# JIRA_API_TOKEN=
# JIRA_PERSONAL_TOKEN=
